<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Burkina Faso</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Burkina Faso is a landlocked country in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a>, with its capital at Ouagadougou. Its central plateau was the home of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mossi">Mossi</a> kingdoms, whose rulers still hold traditional authority, and the country was the French colony of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-volta">Upper Volta</a> before independence in 1960. It took its present name, meaning land of upright people, under Thomas Sankara in 1984.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/burkina-faso.jpg" alt="Burkina Faso" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Drawn by SKopp, rewritten by Gabbe and Андрей Перцев · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Burkina_Faso.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
